# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical .gitignore — Kairos ecosystem
# Source of truth: Foundation Charter v1.2, Part 7.
# Copy this into every new repo. Merge additional app-specific
# rules BELOW the canonical block; never remove or relax a line
# above the "app-specific" divider. `.gitignore` is the boundary-
# enforcement mechanism for version control — not a convenience.
# One copy per GIT REPO, at its root (Part 7: "built once per
# repo") — module folders inside a monorepo carry only their own
# app-specific rules. Decided 2026-07-15; see kairos-system/docs/
# DESIGN_NOTE_gitignore_once_per_repo.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Secrets and credentials — NEVER commit ──
.env
.env.*
*.key
config/*.key
config/*-key.json
config/credentials.json
config/token*.json
config/llm.json          # holds api_key; the gap the Kairos audit caught
*-key.json
*secret*
*credentials*

# ── Databases and their sidecars (may contain sensitive content) ──
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db.bak*
*.bak

# ── Real personal data, fixtures, debug dumps ──
*debug*dump*
*_dump.md
fixtures/real/           # real-data fixtures live here and never sync
emails/
*.eml

# ── Local/machine-specific ──
.claude/settings.local.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
.DS_Store

# ── Encryption keys for at-rest sensitive stores ──
home_kg.key
*.fernet

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# App-specific rules go BELOW this line (add, never subtract).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# kairos-whiteboard is a standalone public repo AND a folder tracked inside kairos_v3
# (the dual-tracked phone-app pattern). App-specific rules: none at the root —
# the Capacitor shell keeps its own build/node_modules rules in native/.gitignore.
